Z||000005||Joe Torma||09-18-2001||02:03 AM||||I've got a comuter nearly installed in my car.  Some other people have been secretly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  putting computers in their cars.<P>I think there are adapters to monitor your stock computer form the ADL connector, but you cannot change parameters.<P>I have an aftermarket engine control system that is programmed and monitored via computer.  Expensive, moderately complicated and incredible.<P>No HP readings through it.  I have a G-tech for that.<P>I'm a ricer?!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||falconhulk||09-18-2001||08:29 AM||||I have a laptop in my car.  Dont use it for all that.  Instead i use it to play MP3's and CD's through the stock radio.  I also use it for navigation.  I have AAA map n go software and a 3 year old GPS with serial hookup so that I can follow my car on the map.  I pulled the pocket from the dash and bolted in supports.  The laptop botton fits flat against the dash.  When I want to use it I flip the screen up to 180 degrees to the bottom.  This puts the keyboard directly infrot of the passanger and the display near the windshield.  To play MP3's and CD's I bought a 10 dollar fm transmitter and hooked it to the laptop.  Just tune to a empty station.  I plan to get a newer laptop soon with DVD capability.  Right now I am pulling it out when I park the car.  I hope to come up with a cover to hide it soon.  Oh yeah look for a laptop that has a DC voltage of between 12V and 13.5.  Some have 17 to 25vdc and would not work off the car battery.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kasdan||09-18-2001||09:36 AM||||Joe Torma - Could you give me a little more info on how you hooked up the computer?  I dont really need to be able to change paramaters, just monitor now that i think about it.  And the mp3 thing is a good idea too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
