Z||000009||Joe Torma||09-18-2001||11:33 AM||||I posted some pics a while ago.  I've been meaning to update...I've done a lot more since then, but I've been busy.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009833.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009833.html</A> <P>It is integrated into the car.  GPS, MP3, Dolby 5.1 DVD, tells me jokes, programs the engine, downloads and my email, etc....Pennocks on the go.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||09-18-2001||11:34 PM||||Well, the laptop won't be totally integrated into the car, but it is there to talk to the Holley Commander 950 aftermarket ECU.  Infact, you have to use a computer to setup and program the fuel maps.<P><BR>Might do the GPS thing too one of these days.<BR>Need to find a card.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
